  "manufactured_solution": "Linear cell scalar q = a·r̂ for the constant cartesian vector a = (1, 0.37, -0.6); on the unit sphere q(lon,lat) = cos(lat)cos(lon) + 0.37·cos(lat)sin(lon) - 0.6·sin(lat). Its surface gradient is the tangential projection of a, so the analytic edge-normal gradient is a·n̂_e, where n̂_e is the tangent-plane projection (at the primal edge midpoint) of the circumcenter-to-circumcenter chord of the edge's two incident triangles, oriented lower→higher face (matching faces_on_edge / edge_sign_on_face). The runner injects q at cell circumcenters, evaluates the discrete edge-normal gradient (q[f_hi]-q[f_lo])/dv_edge, and compares to a·n̂_e.",
